holoscan-rectify uses the following NVIDIA software, and follows the conventions of
OpenCV's calibration module.

Holoscan SDK (https://github.com/nvidia-holoscan/holoscan-sdk)
Copyright (c) NVIDIA CORPORATION & AFFILIATES.
Licensed under Apache-2.0. Linked from the installed SDK; not redistributed.

NVIDIA VPI 4 (optional, for the vpi-* backends)
Copyright (c) NVIDIA CORPORATION & AFFILIATES.
Under NVIDIA's license, installed with VPI as /opt/nvidia/vpi4/doc/VPI_EULA.txt. Linked
from the installed VPI; not redistributed.

OpenCV (https://opencv.org)
The output cameras follow the published methods that OpenCV's getOptimalNewCameraMatrix()
and stereoRectify() implement (Bouguet's rectification), with the same conventions, so
that the results can be compared. No OpenCV code is included or linked; OpenCV is
licensed under Apache-2.0.
